{"archetypes":[{"name":"call-inventory","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan enumerates callers of git-amend-add.sh and drop-bump-commit.sh but does not verify completeness against actual repo evidence; a missed caller leaves the bug unfixed for that execution path.","prompt_body":"Grep the repository for every invocation of git-amend-add.sh and drop-bump-commit.sh, then compare the call sites found against those enumerated in the plan's Files-to-modify list and the rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md prose. Flag any caller present in the codebase but absent from the plan's update list, since each un-migrated git-amend-add.sh call for CHANGELOG would leave the amended-bump bug alive on that path, and each drop-bump-commit.sh call lacking --allow-changelog-only would leave the defense-in-depth incomplete. Also verify that the plan's assertion that git-amend-add.sh has no remaining CHANGELOG callers after the refactor is consistent with what grep finds in scripts/, skills/, and .claude/. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"flag-plumbing","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan adds --allow-changelog-only to drop-bump-commit.sh and states the sub-procedure passes it at step 1, but the original stall occurred when ship-pr.sh's force-push-gate invoked drop-bump-commit.sh internally; if the flag does not reach that internal invocation the defense-in-depth is broken.","prompt_body":"Trace the call chain from the Rebase + Re-bump Sub-procedure's step 1 invocation of drop-bump-commit.sh through to the force-push-gate phase's own invocation of the same script, checking whether --allow-changelog-only is explicitly present on both call sites. Read scripts/drop-bump-commit.sh and skills/implement/references/rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md to verify where the flag is threaded, and check whether ship-pr.sh or any script it delegates to calls drop-bump-commit.sh independently without the flag. If the flag is absent on the force-push-gate invocation, the sub-procedure step 1 setting does not carry over and the stall can recur despite the fix. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"head-ordering","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's correctness depends on the CHANGELOG commit sitting at HEAD and the bump commit at HEAD~1 when drop-bump-commit.sh runs; any intermediate commit between step 4a and the drop invocation, or accumulation across Step 12 CI loop iterations, breaks this FOUND_AT=1 assumption.","prompt_body":"Examine all code paths in implement-finalize.sh, rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md, and ship-pr.sh between the point where commit-changelog.sh creates the CHANGELOG commit and the point where drop-bump-commit.sh is invoked, checking whether any intermediate step could push the bump commit deeper than HEAD~1. Pay special attention to the Step 12 CI loop where multiple iterations each add a bump+CHANGELOG pair, and determine whether drop-bump-commit.sh's --max-depth scan accommodates FOUND_AT greater than 1 due to accumulated CHANGELOG commits. Also verify that the plan's claim 'drop-bump finds the real bump commit at HEAD~1 (FOUND_AT=1)' holds in the multi-iteration sub-procedure context and not only in the single-iteration happy path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
